{"step_index":247,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T12:16:15Z","thinking":"**Investigating SSH key deployment script**\n\nThe script assumes a standard `authorized_keys` file location, but the server uses a potentially different location specified via configuration, or uses a per-user configuration. The SSH daemon also has an `AllowGroups` directive, requiring users to be in a specific group for access. This potentially explains why the current deployment is failing; the generated SSH key might not be placed in the expected location or the user is not in the correct group.\n\n\n**Refining SSH key deployment strategy**\n\nThe `sshd -T` command dynamically resolves the effective `AuthorizedKeysFile` and `AllowGroups` settings, essential for customizing the key deployment process. The bootstrap payload in the script needs to be updated. It should read the results of `sshd -T`, locate the correct file, write the key, and, if `AllowGroups` is configured, add the relevant user to the specified group and the `sudo` group. Also, the standard `~/.ssh/authorized_keys` file must also be updated in parallel.\n\n**Validating deployment logic through testing**\n\nTo test this logic, a new user `koby-bowser-ansible` must be created on a test system, then added to the necessary groups and `sudo` for access. Validating that the script successfully deploys the keys, adds the user to the correct groups based on the `AllowGroups` configuration, and ensures the correct file permissions are set is key to verification. The `authorized_keys` file location from `sshd -T` must be dynamically resolved in the test run.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > /home/koby/.ansible/scripts/copy-to-remote.sh\\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# ==============================================================================\\n# Script: copy-to-remote.sh\\n# Purpose: Ensures 'koby-bowser-ansible' user exists on remote host with\\n#          passwordless SSH (Debian Trixie ed25519 pubkey) and passwordless sudo,\\n#          honoring host sshd configuration (AllowGroups, AuthorizedKeysFile),\\n#          then runs playbooks/copy-to-tmp.yml to copy specified file to /tmp.\\n# Workspace: ~/.ansible\\n# ==============================================================================\\n\\nset -eo pipefail\\n\\n# ANSI Colors (Ubuntu terminal standard)\\nC_RESET=$'\\\\033[0m'\\nC_RED=$'\\\\033[0;31m'\\nC_GREEN=$'\\\\033[0;32m'\\nC_YELLOW=$'\\\\033[0;33m'\\nC_BLUE=$'\\\\033[0;34m'\\nC_BOLD=$'\\\\033[1m'\\n\\nSCRIPT_DIR=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\\\")\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nANSIBLE_DIR=\\\"$(cd \\\"${SCRIPT_DIR}/..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nPLAYBOOK=\\\"${ANSIBLE_DIR}/playbooks/copy-to-tmp.yml\\\"\\n\\nTARGET_USER=\\\"koby-bowser-ansible\\\"\\nPUBKEY_PATH=\\\"${HOME}/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub\\\"\\nPRIVKEY_PATH=\\\"${HOME}/.ssh/id_ed25519\\\"\\nSSH_PORT=\\\"22\\\"\\nADMIN_USER=\\\"root\\\"\\n\\nusage() {\\n    cat << USAGE\\n${C_BOLD}Usage:${C_RESET}\\n    $(basename \\\"$0\\\") [OPTIONS] <REMOTE_HOST> <FILE_PATH>\\n\\n${C_BOLD}Description:${C_RESET}\\n    1. Checks if '${TARGET_USER}' is present on <REMOTE_HOST> with passwordless SSH.\\n    2. If missing, connects via admin user to create '${TARGET_USER}', dynamically\\n       respects sshd AllowGroups & AuthorizedKeysFile, installs your Debian Trixie\\n       ed25519 pubkey, and configures passwordless sudo.\\n    3. Executes '${PLAYBOOK}' to copy <FILE_PATH> to /tmp on <REMOTE_HOST>.\\n\\n${C_BOLD}Arguments:${C_RESET}\\n    <REMOTE_HOST>          Target hostname or IP address\\n    <FILE_PATH>            Local file to copy into remote /tmp\\n\\n${C_BOLD}Options:${C_RESET}\\n    -p, --port <PORT>      SSH port (default: ${SSH_PORT})\\n    -a, --admin <USER>     Admin/bootstrap user if '${TARGET_USER}' needs creation (default: ${ADMIN_USE\n<truncated 7497 bytes>","Cwd":"\"/home/koby/.ansible\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"3000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Update copy-to-remote.sh with AllowGroups and AuthorizedKeysFile logic\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
